BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Out Sports League] Fridays - Draft/REMIX League (A/B/C/D)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260828T182000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260828T210000
UID:Out_Sports_League-Fridays_-_Draft/REMIX_League_(A/B/C/D)-2026-08-28T18
 :20:00
DESCRIPTION:ONLY ACCEPTING PLAYERS INTO THE A/B (ADVANCED/UPPER INTERMEDI
 ATE) DIVISION\nIF YOU REGISTER AS A C/D PLAYER YOU WILL BE PLACED ON THE W
 AIT LIST AND REFUNDED\n\nFRIDAY NIGHTS: DRAFT/REMIX LEAGUE\nWelcome to our
  new Friday Night Draft Indoor Volleyball League\, this league will contai
 n 2 divisions containing of players of the following skill levels:\n\nCOMP
 ETITIVE DIVISION\nA – Advanced. Experienced and competitive players who 
 execute plays consistently at a high level.\nB – Upper Intermediate. Abo
 ve average players who can bump\, set and spike consistently.\n\nRECREATIO
 NAL DIVISION\nC – Lower Intermediate. Improving players who inconsistent
 ly perform 3 hits and can't spike with power.\nD – Novice / Beginner. Re
 creational players who are learning the rules and basic skills of the game
 .\n\nOUT Sports League provides fun\, recreation\, and social sports leagu
 e to Central Florida's LGBTQ+ community. Our Indoor Volleyball league is d
 esigned to be inclusive of people of skill levels and backgrounds. We offe
 r a Social Division (for beginners or players interested in a relaxed\, fu
 n atmosphere)\, and a Competitive Divisions (only players with prior indoo
 r volleyball experience who are secure in the rules are encouraged to play
  in the competitive division). All of our leagues offer a great opportunit
 y to meet other people in our community in a fun\, friendly\, and acceptin
 g atmosphere. Following the games we'll go to District Dive where you'll g
 et a FREE DRINK ticket every week.\n\nThis is a Draft/Remix League where a
 ll players register as an INDIVIDUAL. All players may name one (1) other p
 layer during registration that they'd like to be placed on a team with. Te
 ams will be created by a Captain's Draft or by the League.\n\n❤️ 🧡 
 💛 💚 💙 💜🖤\n\nLEAGUE INFORMATION\n\n8 Week Indoor Volleyball 
 Season\nFridays from July 10 - August 28\nCompetitive (A/B) and Recreation
 al (C/D) Divisions\nMatches will start at 6:20\, 7:10 and 8:00pm\n\n- 12 T
 eams Maximum with divisions determined by registration\n- Recreational Tea
 ms will have 9 players\, Competitive Teams will have 8 players.\n- 6v6 ma
 tches with standard rotating rules\, no libero players and rally scoring\n
 - Games are to 21 (win by 2 or first to 25). Always play all 3 games.\n- A
 ll games are refereed. Each team is required to contribute line judges.\n
 \nGames are played at:\nDover Shores Neighborhood Center\n1400 Gaston Fost
 er Rd\, Orlando\, FL 32812\n\nWeekly after parties at:\nDistrict Dive\n240
 1 E South St\, Orlando\, FL 32803\n\nREGISTRATION INFORMATION\n\n$70 per P
 layer\nLeague Fee Covers - T-Shirt\, Fields\, Equipment\, Umpires\, Photos
 \, Awards\, and Weekly After Party!\n\nINDIVIDUAL - All players register a
 s an Individual. When league registration closes you will placed on a tea
 m.\n\nWant to play with a friend?\nIn a Draft/Remix Season players are per
 mitted to list one (1) other player that they'd like to be placed on a tea
 m with. Please make sure you and your friend list each other when prompted
  during registration. Chains of friends are not permitted.\n\nFAQ\n\nI do
 n't have a team\, can I still play?\nYes\, register as an Individual and w
 e will place you with a team.\n\nI will miss a few weeks\, can I still pla
 y?\nYes\, all teams have extra players on them just in case you're absent 
 on a given week. Teams can also use substitute players.\n\nHow do I make s
 ure my friend and I play on the same team?\nDuring registration there is a
  field where you can list the friend you want to play with and the league 
 will place you together.\n\nI don't know how to play or don't think I'll b
 e very good\, should I play?\nYes\, join our Wednesday or Friday Night lea
 gues aimed at new and developing players and you will learn the basics in 
 a fun\, encouraging environment.\n\nI'm not LGBTQ+\, can I still play?\nYe
 s\, we are accepting to all people as long as you consider yourself an all
 y to our community.\n\nMore info: https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/l
 eagues/volleyball-(indoor)/5048670-fridays---draftremix-league-abcd
LOCATION:Dover Shores Community Center
URL:https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/504
 8670-fridays---draftremix-league-abcd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Out Sports League] Tuedays - Recreational (C/D)
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T182000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261020T210000
UID:Out_Sports_League-Tuedays_-_Recreational_(C/D)-2026-10-20T18:20:00
DESCRIPTION:TUESDAY NIGHTS: RECREATIONAL LEAGUE\n*There is one week (11/11
 ) where games will be on a Wednesday instead!\n\nWelcome to our new Tuesda
 y Night Recreational Indoor Volleyball League\, this is a Recreational lea
 gue for players of the following skill levels:\n\nC – Lower Intermediate
 . Improving players who inconsistently perform 3 hits and can't spike with
  power.\nD – Novice / Beginner. Recreational players who are learning th
 e rules and basic skills of the game.\n\nIf you're a competitive player pl
 ease register for our Thursday or Friday night leagues. \n\nOUT Sports Le
 ague provides fun\, recreation\, and social sports league to Central Flori
 da's LGBTQ+ community. Our Indoor Volleyball league is designed to be incl
 usive of people of skill levels and backgrounds. All of our leagues offer 
 a great opportunity to meet other people in our community in a fun\, frien
 dly\, and accepting atmosphere. Following the games we'll go to District D
 ive where you'll get a FREE DRINK ticket every week. This season is sponso
 red by Pineapple Healthcare.\n\nCreate a TEAM! On Wednesdays you can becom
 e a TEAM CAPTAIN and have your players register as TEAM PLAYERS. Please no
 te our leagues have a fixed capacity of 100 players\, if your team is inco
 mplete when registration closes or capacity is reached the league will add
  free agents to your team.\n\nDon't have a Team? Register as a FREE AGENT 
 and we will place you on a team. Free agents can also name a FRIEND(S) tha
 t they want to play with and the league will place you together.\n\n❤️
  🧡 💛 💚 💙 💜🖤\n\nLEAGUE INFORMATION\n\n8 Week Indoor Volle
 yball Season\nTuesdays from October 20 - December 15\nWeek 4 games will ta
 ke place on Wednesday\, November 11\nMatches will start at 6:20\, 7:10 an
 d 8:00pm\n\n- Players must be Beginner\, Novice or Lower Intermediate Skil
 l Levels (C/D).\n- 10 Teams Maximum. Recreational Teams must have 9 playe
 rs.\n- 6v6 matches with standard rotating rules\, no libero players and ra
 lly scoring.\n- Games are to 21 (win by 2 or first to 25). Always play all
  3 games.\n- All games are refereed. Each team is required to contribute l
 ine judges.\n\nGames are played at:\nDr James R Smith Center\n1723 Bruton 
 Blvd\, Orlando\, FL 32805\n\nWeekly after parties at:\nDistrict Dive\n2401
  E South St\, Orlando\, FL 32803\n\nREGISTRATION INFORMATION\n\n$70 per Pl
 ayer\nLeague Fee Covers - T-Shirt\, Fields\, Equipment\, Umpires\, Photos
 \, Awards\, and Weekly After Party!\n\nTEAM CAPTAIN* - Create a team of 9+
  and invite your friends!\nTEAM PLAYER - Join an existing team (please onl
 y join if invited to a team)\nFREE AGENT - Don't have a team? No problem! 
 Register without a team and you can list friends you want to play with. Wh
 en league registration closes you will placed on a team.\n\nWant to play w
 ith a few friends?\nIf you have a buddy or a small group of friends who wa
 nt to play together you can all register as Free Agents. During registrati
 on you will be prompted to list player(s) that you'd like to play with. Ev
 eryone should register separately and the league will then place you and y
 our friends together on a team.\n\n* Please note the league has a fixed ca
 pacity of 90 players\, if your team is incomplete when registration closes
  or capacity is reached the league will add free agents to your team.\n\nF
 AQ\n\nI don't have a team\, can I still play?\nYes\, register as an Indivi
 dual and we will place you with a team.\n\nI will miss a few weeks\, can I
  still play?\nYes\, all teams have extra players on them just in case you'
 re absent on a given week. Teams can also use substitute players.\n\nHow d
 o I make sure my friend and I play on the same team?\nDuring registration 
 there is a field where you can list the friend(s) you want to play with an
 d the league will place you together.\n\nI don't know how to play or don't
  think I'll be very good\, should I play?\nYes\, join our Wednesday or Fri
 day Night leagues aimed at new and developing players and you will learn 
 the basics in a fun\, encouraging environment.\n\nI'm not LGBTQ+\, can I s
 till play?\nYes\, we are accepting to all people as long as you consider y
 ourself an ally to our community.\n\nMore info: https://outsportsleague.le
 agueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/5151697-tuedays---recreational-cd
LOCATION:Dr. James R. Smith Center
URL:https://outsportsleague.leagueapps.com/leagues/volleyball-(indoor)/515
 1697-tuedays---recreational-cd
END:VEVENT
